{"type":"text","timestamp":1794255950148,"sessionID":"ses_e3e0b2786ffein4CQhbx5fjWsf","part":{"id":"prt_1c1fd1130001rc5ek63YBHancs","messageID":"msg_1c1fced80001gnhsRGgZnxPUHM","sessionID":"ses_e3e0b2786ffein4CQhbx5fjWsf","type":"text","text":"The reservation app is built: a Flask API with SQLite in `backend/app.py` and a React + TypeScript + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. I couldn't build or run the Docker image because Docker isn't installed here. Instead I tested the API locally under gunicorn and with Flask's test client, and the frontend passes `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build`. I didn't click through the web UI in a browser.\n\n**What the local tests confirmed:**\n- **Seat limit:** 12 bookings of 2 guests sent at the same moment to one slot gave 10 successes and 2 refusals, ending at exactly 20 booked. Over-limit bookings and changes get a 409 with a message like \"Not enough seats left at 19:00 on 2026-12-01: 5 of 20 remaining, 6 requested.\" The booking form shows that message.\n- **Changing a reservation:** its own guests aren't counted twice, and leaving out `notes` clears it.\n- **Other users' reservations:** reading, changing or cancelling one answers 404, as if it didn't exist.\n- **Sign-in:** requests without a valid token get 401; a normal user calling the admin endpoint gets 403.\n- **Admin:** `admin` signs in only when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is set; with it unset, admin sign-in is refused. Admin paging works.\n- **Availability:** `GET /api/availability` lists booked slots with `booked` and `remaining`.\n\n**Behaviour you might not expect:**\n- `GET /api/availability` without a `date` uses today's date rather than returning an error.\n- Passwords must be at least 8 characters. Nobody can register the name `admin`.\n- Tokens last 30 days, and the frontend keeps the token in the browser's local storage.\n\n**Additions beyond the spec:**\n- `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me`.\n- Admin list items also carry a `username` field, and the admin response includes `total_guests`.\n- `GET /api/availability` also returns `date` and `capacity`.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- Frontend dependencies are pinned in `package.json`, and `package-lock.json` is updated. Backend requirements are unchanged.\n- I added a `.gitignore`, added the local Python environment to `.dockerignore`, and added a short API section to `README.md`.\n- A Python virtual environment is left at `/workspace/.venv` from testing; it's ignored by git and excluded from the Docker build.","time":{"start":1794255950128,"end":1794255950131}}}
